{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts security deposit limits","requirement":"A landlord may hold a security deposit of at most one month's rent, keep it in a separate interest-bearing account, pay 5% interest a year, give receipts and a statement of condition, and return the deposit with an itemized list of deductions within 30 days after the tenancy ends.","key_value":"1 month's rent","coverage_conditions":"Residential real property leases.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Successor-in-interest deposit liability does not apply to a city or town acquiring title under chapter 60, or to a foreclosing mortgagee or mortgagee in possession that is a chartered financial institution.","penalty":"Landlord forfeits the right to retain any part of the deposit; tenant awarded three times the deposit plus 5% interest, court costs and attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(iii) a security deposit equal to the first month's rent provided that such security deposit is deposited as required by subsection (3) and that the tenant is given the statement of condition as required by subsection (2);","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts cap on upfront charges","requirement":"A landlord or agent may not require a tenant or applicant to pay more than first month's rent, last month's rent, a security deposit equal to one month's rent, and key and lock costs, and may not demand rent in advance beyond the current month's rent.","key_value":"first + last month's rent + 1 month deposit + key/lock cost","coverage_conditions":"Any tenancy in residential real property; binds lessors and their agents.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(b) At or prior to the commencement of any tenancy, no lessor or agent of the lessor may require a tenant or prospective tenant to pay, to the lessor or to an agent of the lessor, any amount in excess of the following:","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts fee-in-lieu-of-deposit applicant protections","requirement":"A landlord who offers a fee in lieu of a security deposit must offer it to every approved applicant regardless of income, credit score and other listed traits, and may not use those factors to set the fee amount.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Lessors who offer a fee in lieu of a security deposit to approved applicants.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(I) to offer the option of a fee in lieu of a security deposit to every prospective tenant whose application for occupancy has been approved, regardless of income, race, gender, gender identity, disability, sexual orientation, immigration status, size of household or credit score;  and (II) not to consider such factors and categories when setting the amount of the fee;","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","n_rules":3,"note":null}

